00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,000
Most of the time, the market is will spend their time in balance.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,200
That's why the markets are invented, to facilitate trade.

24
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,800
When markets are facilitating trade, the markets are in balance.

25
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:43,400
Buyers and sellers are happy.

26
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:50,700
When the market starts to move out of balance, that's when moves start to occur, trends start to occur.

27
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,600
And that's where you're going to get your biggest trading opportunities.

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,545
If you're trading at a level where price is accepted

29
00:01:59,545 --> 00:02:01,317
and everyone's happy to trade,

30
00:02:01,317 --> 00:02:03,798
then the market's not going to move.

31
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,300
It's when one side starts to take over.

32
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:11,500
Maybe there's a shortage that somebody knows about that hasn't necessarily hit the market.

33
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:14,600
You're going to see the people with that information come

34
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,100
into the market and move

35
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,800
the market. It's starting to move out of balance.

36
00:02:22,848 --> 00:02:23,934
So, you know, in a

37
00:02:23,934 --> 00:02:25,455
basic sense, why does the market move

38
00:02:25,455 --> 00:02:27,846
out of balance is the question you want to be asking.

39
00:02:28,348 --> 00:02:35,848
You know, in a simple form, it's buyers are overwhelming sellers or sellers are overwhelming buyers.

40
00:02:36,348 --> 00:02:38,075
What that means is, you

41
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:40,493
know, there's at any given moment you

42
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:43,947
have a group of buyers and a group of sellers.

43
00:02:45,948 --> 00:02:48,766
The group of buyers really get interested in buying and

44
00:02:48,766 --> 00:02:51,020
they buy all the supply that the sellers

45
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:55,247
have to offer, the price is going to start to move to a higher price.

46
00:02:57,148 --> 00:02:59,848
People are being more aggressive and the market is starting to rally.

47
00:03:00,748 --> 00:03:05,648
And conversely, when sellers are overwhelming the buyers, maybe there's a lot of inventory on the market.

48
00:03:06,748 --> 00:03:10,348
That's going to be hitting the market rather, not necessarily on the market at the moment.

49
00:03:10,448 --> 00:03:12,848
But if there even is a lot of

50
00:03:12,848 --> 00:03:14,648
inventory currently in the market and

51
00:03:14,648 --> 00:03:17,648
it's not being sold, people have to lower their price.

52
00:03:18,348 --> 00:03:21,248
And they'll lower their price until they can find buyers.

53
00:03:21,948 --> 00:03:23,748
Mark, that's what causes the market to sell off.

54
00:03:23,748 --> 00:03:24,386
You know,

55
00:03:24,386 --> 00:03:25,344
imagine it, you

56
00:03:25,344 --> 00:03:26,941
know, if you're a department

57
00:03:26,941 --> 00:03:28,538
store and, you know, you

58
00:03:28,538 --> 00:03:30,135
bought a lot of winter

59
00:03:30,135 --> 00:03:35,246
coats and now it's, you know, it's March and the weather is starting to get warm.

60
00:03:35,948 --> 00:03:38,248
You have a lot of inventory of winter coats.

61
00:03:38,248 --> 00:03:39,548
You've got to start lowering the price.

62
00:03:39,548 --> 00:03:40,548
You've got to start moving them.

63
00:03:44,508 --> 00:03:49,708
When traders talk about a market being imbalanced, they often think the market is moving in a sideways direction.

64
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:50,808
That's not always the case.

65
00:03:51,808 --> 00:03:57,008
The market could be gradually trending higher on slightly heavier buying or lower on slightly heavier selling.

66
00:03:57,208 --> 00:04:02,808
It doesn't have to be overwhelming amounts of buying or selling, just enough to move the market away from balance.

67
00:04:03,208 --> 00:04:08,308
What that means is... A market doesn't have to be trading in an extremely tight range.

68
00:04:08,308 --> 00:04:10,508
A market is going to move up and down just naturally.

69
00:04:11,208 --> 00:04:13,708
A market very rarely stays at one price.

70
00:04:14,708 --> 00:04:18,008
It might be just small fluctuations.

71
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:24,308
Small fluctuations, when they turn into big fluctuations, that's when the market is starting to move out of balance.

72
00:04:24,908 --> 00:04:30,408
So even though a market appears to be in balance and moving sideways, oftentimes one side is in control.

73
00:04:31,108 --> 00:04:33,508
Then the other side takes control, you know, back and forth.

74
00:04:33,608 --> 00:04:38,108
So, you know, people talk about choppy markets.

75
00:04:38,508 --> 00:04:43,608
And, you know, a market is choppy when you get one side, you know, you get buyers.

76
00:04:44,608 --> 00:04:45,701
Seemingly taking control, then

77
00:04:45,701 --> 00:04:47,887
it gets to a level that's not too

78
00:04:47,887 --> 00:04:49,527
far away from where you're currently

79
00:04:49,527 --> 00:04:52,807
trading, then the sellers come in and move it back down again.

80
00:04:54,008 --> 00:04:59,508
A market is in balance in a general area where buyers and sellers are in relative agreement of price.

81
00:04:59,808 --> 00:05:01,508
Like I said, it doesn't have to be one price.

82
00:05:02,308 --> 00:05:10,808
S&Ps could be trading at $1,900, but it could be range trading between $1,905 and, say, $1,897.

83
00:05:11,808 --> 00:05:12,408
It's in a range.

84
00:05:12,408 --> 00:05:13,808
It's not sticking to one price.

85
00:05:13,908 --> 00:05:15,008
It's sticking to an area.

86
00:05:16,508 --> 00:05:20,008
Don't think of it as trading in one particular price.

87
00:05:20,208 --> 00:05:27,508
It could be fluctuating up and down, above the perceived value for the moment.

88
00:05:28,408 --> 00:05:36,008
But when it starts to move away very dramatically, that's when... That's when a market is out of balance.

89
00:05:37,808 --> 00:05:43,908
You know, this picture I like. It's a tank, you know, basically going over a small wall.

90
00:05:44,308 --> 00:05:49,808
And, you know, when a market starts to move out of balance, that's what it's like to me.

91
00:05:50,608 --> 00:05:51,338
You know, where

92
00:05:51,338 --> 00:05:53,042
one side is just basically overwhelms the

93
00:05:53,042 --> 00:05:54,502
other and, you know, it's going

94
00:05:54,502 --> 00:05:56,206
to take a lot to stop it.

95
00:05:56,508 --> 00:05:59,108
You know, in this case, it'll probably take a bazooka to stop this tank.

96
00:06:01,568 --> 00:06:05,568
So when a market imbalance occurs, there's one side that is showing its strength.

97
00:06:07,168 --> 00:06:11,668
And the market should continue in that direction until the new balance is found.

98
00:06:11,768 --> 00:06:19,168
So a market will move from an area of price congestion or price absorption.

99
00:06:19,868 --> 00:06:23,968
To the next area of price congestion or price absorption.

100
00:06:25,768 --> 00:06:30,368
When it moves from the first level to the second level, that's when the imbalance occurs.

101
00:06:31,268 --> 00:06:35,168
Order flows will allow you to pick up on the imbalances in the market as they're occurring.

102
00:06:35,868 --> 00:06:41,068
It's not going to tell you after the move has already happened. It's telling you as the move is happening.

103
00:06:43,232 --> 00:06:48,232
And generally speaking, a market will trade in balance most of the time.

104
00:06:48,332 --> 00:06:53,832
Like I said, a market range trades about 70% to 80% of the time.

105
00:06:54,032 --> 00:06:56,832
It trends 20% of the time.

106
00:06:57,632 --> 00:07:00,332
Trend followers make their money when the market is trending.

107
00:07:01,032 --> 00:07:05,132
But unfortunately, markets don't generally trend all the time.

108
00:07:05,332 --> 00:07:08,832
They spend most of the time. In balance in a range.

109
00:07:09,432 --> 00:07:12,932
So what causes markets to experience an imbalance?

110
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:15,732
Well, I mean, there's a lot of things that can happen.

111
00:07:16,632 --> 00:07:20,832
You know, new fundamentals can hit the market that, you know, you don't necessarily see.

112
00:07:20,932 --> 00:07:23,532
All you're going to see is the after effect in the market.

113
00:07:24,132 --> 00:07:25,532
You know, you may...

114
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:36,180
Like I said, most traders don't necessarily have access to fundamental data that the big traders have.

115
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:38,830
So you're not going to know

116
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:41,280
what's causing it, but what you

117
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:46,180
