stop gets triggered, there's a bunch

127
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:25,680
of orders going to be triggered and go through the market.

128
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:31,480
It's going to basically, a stop will turn whatever's there into a market order.

129
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:35,480
And it'll just sweep the entire book until it stops.

130
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:41,980
And then either more buyers or more sellers will come into the market to add liquidity.

131
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:45,980
Big orders hitting the market will also cause imbalances.

132
